      ":question/id": "2f3cf3eb-fe31-58ef-a584-753c041d9334",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5u - 4v &=-9 \\\\ -5u + 8v &=-21\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $v$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $v$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that the coefficient of $v$ in the first equation is $-4$, while in the second equation it is $8$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}2}$, then the coefficient of $v$ will turn into $-8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $8$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}&(-5u - 4v = -9)\\cdot (2) \\\\ &-5u + 8v = -21\\end{aligned}\\right.\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-10u - 8v &=-18 \\\\ -5u + 8v &=-21\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $v$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-10u - \\cancel{8v} &= -18 \\\\\n-5u + \\cancel{8v} &= -21 \\\\\n(-10u - 5u) &= (-18 - 21) \\\\\n-15u &= -39\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $v$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2}$, and add the equations*.",
